{"tool_name":"gt-pro","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:gt-pro"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"gt-pro","home":"https://github.com/zjshi/gt-pro","license":"MIT","summary":"Ultra-rapid metagenotyping of the human gut microbiome.\n\nGT-Pro - the GenoTyper for PROkaryotes.\n\nUltra-rapid genotyping of prokaryotes in shotgun metagenomes.\n\nTo genotype a microbiome, GT-Pro takes as input one or more shotgun metagenomics sequencing libraries in FASTQ format. It returns counts of reads exactly matching each allele of each SNP in a concise table-shaped format for its output, with one row for each bi-allelic SNP site that has exactly 8 fields: species, SNP ID, contig, contig position, allele 1, allele 2 and coverage of allele 1 and coverage of allele 2. The k-mer exact match based genotyping algorithm is optimized for machine specificiations, and it can run on a personal computer.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:45:34Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:22:28.853950Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:gt-pro","credit":[{"email":"katherine.pollard@gladstone.ucsf.edu","name":"Katherine S. Pollard","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome indexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3211"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"},{"term":"SNP detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484"}]}],"name":"GT-Pro","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41587-021-01102-3","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1101/2020.06.12.149336","type":["Preprint"]}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Metagenomic sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3837"},{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"},